# Derived data and model weights are reproducible from the fetchers; never commit them.
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. A bare "data/" also matches
# src/seam/data/, which silently left six source modules untracked - the data
# acquisition package was invisible to git while existing on disk.
artifacts/
/data/
# SignStream XML annotations. The ASLLRP terms say the data "cannot be redistributed
# without permission", and that covers the annotations as well as the video. The anchor on
# /data/ above is the real protection; this is a second net, because the licence
# consequence of a stray `git add` is worse than the inconvenience of ignoring a file
# type that no source file in this repo uses.
*.xml
*.npz
*.npy
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.parquet
*.mp4
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
!paper/figures/*.png
# Report figures and demo screenshots: generated from artifacts, shown in README and the site.
!docs/figures/*.png

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
.env

# Node
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# LaTeX
paper/main.aux
paper/main.bbl
paper/main.blg
paper/main.fdb_latexmk
paper/main.fls
paper/main.log
paper/main.out
paper/main.synctex.gz
paper/main.pdf

# W&B
wandb/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
